From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] prime, tides: foreign canaries cluster gateways on one
 template source (SOV-015)

An own canary's twin C' can also go to other gateways' registered nodes. Primed
records a foreign canary for each such target (POST /sovereignty/canary
"foreign": [G2, ...]) and schedules the target's check too. A target whose
checked job carries C shares a template source with the canary's gateway.

entropy: CanaryKind::Foreign, per-source SourceTally, shared_sources (single
linkage on due >= CANARY_MIN, hits >= 3, rate >= 0.25) and
apply_shared_sources: independence / n across the cluster and reason
shared-template-source, without setting flagged. Tests: honest gateways with
relay jitter never cluster (20 seeds), three on one node are one cluster,
mixed farms, late twins would cluster honest gateways.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
