+//! * **Foreign canaries** (SOV-015; cluster only). An own canary C for gateway G whose twin C′ was
+//!   also delivered, right after C, to the registered nodes of other gateways. Those nodes hold C′
+//!   and reject C when it relays in, so an honest G2 never templates C. A G2 whose template carries
+//!   C builds from a source that got C, and so shares it with G's node. Gateways that carry each
+//!   other's canaries are one *shared-template-source* cluster ([`shared_sources`]): independence
+//!   is split `1/n` across it, and nobody is flagged for it.
+//!
 //! Together these corner a hybrid (pool template + its own node's mempool). Own canaries force it
 //! to take its node's side of a conflict. Decoys force it to drop what its node lacks (T ⊆ L).
 //! Shared canaries force it to keep what its node has, even where the pool left it out (T ⊇ L).
