+/// holds the twin C′ before C can relay in, so its rate is the relay-race rate (measured ≈ 0).
+/// A gateway on G's source carries G's canary exactly when G hits its own, so a shared source
+/// can push this under the bar only by pushing G's own hit rate there too.
+pub const FOREIGN_FLAG: f64 = 0.25;
+/// Foreign hits one source must reach besides the rate, so a couple of relay-race losses at
+/// low due never join two honest gateways.
+pub const FOREIGN_MIN_HITS: usize = 3;
 
